   "user": "Defender",
   "message": "The Hank Green scandal itself is something that could have been engineered - all it required was\n\n- finding an angle, Hank Green says something innocuous in a video, you can clip it, and tweet it and say \"omg hank forgot to remove the LLM line from his script\"\n- you @ the right people, who retweet it\n- the basic level is a few people responding to this narrative\n- the \"success\" is him having to respond to it\n\nbut if someone did this during the event I would consider it an \"illegal move\" (hurts the epistemic commons more than it helps it)",
   "timestamp": "2026-08-05T14:26:50.708000+00:00",
   "channel": "the-september-event",
